{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_inmemorycache", "label": "InMemoryCache", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/in-memory.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The default Cache: a Map with LRU eviction, lazy per-entry TTL and an optional background sweep. Single-process only, so multi-pod deployments each keep their own copy; setIfAbsent is atomic here for a structural reason (read and write in one synchronous block) rather than a protocol one."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_inmemorycacheoptions", "label": "InMemoryCacheOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/in-memory.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "maxEntries (default 10000) and cleanupMs (default 60000), validated once at construction on the merged settings so the builder, a plain object and HOCON all hit the same check and a bad value throws OptionsError."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_lru_eviction", "label": "LRU eviction bounded by maxEntries", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/in-memory.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keeps a flood of distinct never-re-read keys (attacker-chosen idempotency or rate-limit keys) from growing the map without limit. Only a read counts as a use, so an entry written once and never read back ages towards eviction from the moment it is stored."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_guarantee_carrying_entries", "label": "Guarantee-carrying cache entries", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/in-memory.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A setIfAbsent claim or an incr counter with a finite TTL: for these the cache IS the source of truth, so losing one voids a guarantee rather than costing a round-trip. A set picks a guarantee up only when it replaces a live claim under the same key, which is the shape idempotent uses; a claim with no TTL is not protected, because protecting one would make it permanent."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_opportunistic_entries", "label": "Opportunistic cache entries", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/in-memory.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Everything written by set or mset has a source of truth behind it, so losing one is a cache miss the caller already handles; eviction drains this half first, least-recently-used end onwards."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_dropped_guarantee_cost", "label": "What a dropped guarantee costs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/in-memory.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nothing surfaces when the cap reaches one: a rate limit resets without anyone hitting it, an idempotency record vanishes so an honest retry runs the handler twice (a double charge on payments), and a lock is handed out twice while the original holder is still inside the critical section. The holder's release() then returns false, which reads like a TTL overrun and here means the opposite."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_one_cache_per_consumer", "label": "One cache per consumer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/in-memory.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The eviction policy only re-orders victims inside one instance and does not rank guarantees against each other, so each named cache gets its own instance and its own maxEntries under its own HOCON block, per-name winning over global leaf by leaf. It narrows the blast radius rather than removing it: a consumer whose own key space is attacker-controlled can still evict its own entries."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_ttl_handling", "label": "Lazy TTL with a background sweep", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/in-memory.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Expiry is checked on every read path, and a sweep every cleanupMs reclaims expired entries nothing touches again so they do not sit in the Map waiting for a read; setting cleanupMs to 0 or Infinity relies on lazy expiry alone."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_inmemorycache", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_overview_cache_interface", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/in-memory.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_inmemorycache", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_inmemorycacheoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/in-memory.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_inmemorycache", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_lru_eviction", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cache/in-memory.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_inmemorycache", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cache_in_memory_ttl_handling", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": 